all with far more cash on hand. Expert raters split between Likely R and Solid or Safe R, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-six chance.\n\nThe only available poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from May 2025, showed Van Drew ahead by ten points, though it is dated and hypothetical. A Democratic-leaning national environment and Mullock's primary win give the challenger some room, but the money gap, incumbency, and district lean point to a clear Republican advantage. A scheduled debate and any late outside spending are the main remaining variables.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1228, "margin": -7.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1056, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0906, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -9.0}]}